# Logical data model

## Entity: `UserProfile`
- Purpose: Identify an authenticated product participant for scope and display.
- Ownership: Repository-owned access control, referenced by Aug1.
- Keys: `id` primary key.
- Foreign keys: `organisationId` targets the institution identity boundary.
- Uniqueness: `id` is unique.
- Enums: `participantType` is Teacher, Coordinator, Student, or Administrator.
- Concurrency: none.
- Sensitive data: name and institutional affiliation.
- Lifecycle: Active to Inactive.
- Indexes: query `organisationId, participantType, status`.
- Retention: repository identity retention policy.
- Delete behavior: restrict while referenced by product records.
- Audit: access-control audit owns identity changes.
| Field | Type | Required | Nullable | Default | Constraints | Sensitive | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | UUID | yes | no | supplied by identity | PK, immutable UUIDv7 | internal | Participant identity. |
| organisationId | UUID | yes | no | supplied by identity | institution scope identifier | internal | Institution boundary. |
| displayName | string | yes | no | none | 1–120 characters | personal | Name shown to permitted users. |
| participantType | enum | yes | no | none | Teacher, Coordinator, Student, Administrator | internal | Conceptual participant classification. |
| status | enum | yes | no | Active | Active, Inactive | internal | Identity availability state. |

## Entity: `ClassGroup`
- Purpose: Represent one PE teaching group for an academic term.
- Ownership: Physical Education teaching team.
- Keys: `id` primary key; `code` alternate key within `organisationId`.
- Foreign keys: `organisationId` targets the institution boundary; `leadTeacherId` targets `UserProfile.id`.
- Uniqueness: `organisationId, code` is unique.
- Enums: `status` is Active or Archived.
- Concurrency: `rowVersion` uses optimistic concurrency.
- Sensitive data: internal teaching allocation.
- Lifecycle: Active to Archived.
- Indexes: unique `organisationId, code`; query `organisationId, leadTeacherId, status, academicTerm`.
- Retention: seven years after academic year closes.
- Delete behavior: restrict while enrollments or assessments exist.
- Audit: creation, update, archive, and denied access.
| Field | Type | Required | Nullable | Default | Constraints | Sensitive | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | UUID | yes | no | generated | PK, immutable UUIDv7 | internal | Class group identity. |
| organisationId | UUID | yes | no | context supplied | institution scope identifier | internal | Owning institution. |
| code | string | yes | no | none | 2–20 uppercase letters, digits, or hyphens; unique with organisationId | internal | Human-recognisable class code. |
| title | string | yes | no | none | 1–120 characters | internal | Class display name. |
| activity | string | yes | no | none | 1–80 characters | internal | PE activity or unit. |
| academicTerm | string | yes | no | none | `YYYY-TN`, N is 1–4 | internal | Term identifier. |
| leadTeacherId | UUID | yes | no | actor id | FK UserProfile.id | personal | Teacher accountable for the class. |
| status | enum | yes | no | Active | Active, Archived | internal | Class lifecycle state. |
| createdAt | timestamp | yes | no | generated UTC | immutable after creation | internal | Creation time. |
| updatedAt | timestamp | yes | no | generated UTC | updated on mutation | internal | Last update time. |
| rowVersion | integer | yes | no | generated | positive, incremented on mutation | internal | Optimistic concurrency token. |

## Entity: `Enrollment`
- Purpose: Connect one student to one class group.
- Ownership: Physical Education teaching team.
- Keys: `id` primary key; `classGroupId, studentId` alternate key.
- Foreign keys: `classGroupId` targets `ClassGroup.id`; `studentId` targets `UserProfile.id`.
- Uniqueness: `classGroupId, studentId` is unique.
- Enums: `status` is Active or Inactive.
- Concurrency: none.
- Sensitive data: student participation.
- Lifecycle: Active to Inactive.
- Indexes: unique `classGroupId, studentId`; query `studentId, status`.
- Retention: seven years after academic year closes.
- Delete behavior: restrict while assessments exist.
- Audit: activation and inactivation.
| Field | Type | Required | Nullable | Default | Constraints | Sensitive | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | UUID | yes | no | generated | PK, immutable UUIDv7 | internal | Enrollment identity. |
| classGroupId | UUID | yes | no | none | FK ClassGroup.id | internal | Enrolled class group. |
| studentId | UUID | yes | no | none | FK UserProfile.id; participantType Student | personal | Enrolled student. |
| status | enum | yes | no | Active | Active, Inactive | internal | Enrollment availability. |
| enrolledAt | timestamp | yes | no | generated UTC | immutable after creation | internal | Enrollment start time. |

## Entity: `Assessment`
- Purpose: Persist one educator observation of one active student enrollment.
- Ownership: Physical Education teaching team.
- Keys: `id` primary key.
- Foreign keys: `organisationId` targets institution boundary; `classGroupId` targets `ClassGroup.id`; `enrollmentId` targets `Enrollment.id`; `studentId` targets `UserProfile.id`; `assessedByUserId` targets `UserProfile.id`.
- Uniqueness: none.
- Enums: `status` is Draft, FeedbackReady, or Published.
- Concurrency: `rowVersion` uses optimistic concurrency.
- Sensitive data: student educational observation.
- Lifecycle: Draft to FeedbackReady to Published.
- Indexes: query `organisationId, classGroupId, studentId, assessmentDate`; query `assessedByUserId, status`.
- Retention: seven years after academic year closes.
- Delete behavior: restrict after feedback publication; delete draft only before a feedback draft exists.
- Audit: creation, feedback readiness, publication, and denied access.
| Field | Type | Required | Nullable | Default | Constraints | Sensitive | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | UUID | yes | no | generated | PK, immutable UUIDv7 | internal | Assessment identity. |
| organisationId | UUID | yes | no | context supplied | institution scope identifier | internal | Owning institution. |
| classGroupId | UUID | yes | no | none | FK ClassGroup.id | internal | Observed class group. |
| enrollmentId | UUID | yes | no | none | FK Enrollment.id; must match classGroupId and studentId | internal | Active enrollment assessed. |
| studentId | UUID | yes | no | derived from enrollment | FK UserProfile.id; must match enrollmentId | personal | Assessed student. |
| assessmentDate | date | yes | no | current local date | not future; within class academic term | personal | Observation date. |
| skillLevel | integer | yes | no | none | inclusive range 1–5 | educational | Teacher-selected performance level. |
| observationNote | string | yes | no | none | 20–1,000 characters | educational | Factual teacher observation. |
| assessedByUserId | UUID | yes | no | actor id | FK UserProfile.id; teacher or coordinator in scope | personal | Recording educator. |
| status | enum | yes | no | Draft | Draft, FeedbackReady, Published | internal | Assessment lifecycle state. |
| createdAt | timestamp | yes | no | generated UTC | immutable after creation | internal | Creation time. |
| updatedAt | timestamp | yes | no | generated UTC | updated on mutation | internal | Last update time. |
| rowVersion | integer | yes | no | generated | positive, incremented on mutation | internal | Optimistic concurrency token. |

## Entity: `FeedbackDraft`
- Purpose: Hold the generated and educator-approved feedback for one assessment.
- Ownership: Physical Education teaching team.
- Keys: `id` primary key; `assessmentId` alternate key.
- Foreign keys: `assessmentId` targets `Assessment.id`; `publishedByUserId` targets `UserProfile.id`.
- Uniqueness: `assessmentId` is unique.
- Enums: `generationStatus` is NotRequested, PendingReview, Failed, or Published.
- Concurrency: `rowVersion` uses optimistic concurrency.
- Sensitive data: student educational feedback and generated wording.
- Lifecycle: NotRequested to PendingReview or Failed; PendingReview to Published.
- Indexes: unique `assessmentId`; query `generationStatus, publishedAt`.
- Retention: seven years after academic year closes.
- Delete behavior: restrict after publication; delete draft only with un-published assessment deletion.
- Audit: generation request, generation result, edit, publication, and failed publication.
| Field | Type | Required | Nullable | Default | Constraints | Sensitive | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | UUID | yes | no | generated | PK, immutable UUIDv7 | internal | Feedback draft identity. |
| assessmentId | UUID | yes | no | none | FK Assessment.id; unique | internal | Associated assessment. |
| generationStatus | enum | yes | no | NotRequested | NotRequested, PendingReview, Failed, Published | internal | Draft lifecycle state. |
| generatedText | string | no | yes | none | 1–2,000 characters when present | educational | Proposed AI feedback. |
| educatorEditedText | string | no | yes | none | 1–2,000 characters when present; required to publish | educational | Educator-approved editable text. |
| publishedText | string | no | yes | none | 1–2,000 characters when published; immutable once set | educational | Student-visible approved feedback. |
| generatedAt | timestamp | no | yes | none | UTC when generation succeeds | internal | Generation completion time. |
| publishedAt | timestamp | no | yes | none | UTC when published | internal | Publication time. |
| publishedByUserId | UUID | no | yes | none | FK UserProfile.id when published | personal | Publishing educator. |
| rowVersion | integer | yes | no | generated | positive, incremented on mutation | internal | Optimistic concurrency token. |

## Entity: `FeedbackAcknowledgement`
- Purpose: Record a student’s acknowledgement of published feedback.
- Ownership: Student and Physical Education teaching team.
- Keys: `id` primary key; `feedbackDraftId` alternate key.
- Foreign keys: `feedbackDraftId` targets `FeedbackDraft.id`; `studentId` targets `UserProfile.id`.
- Uniqueness: `feedbackDraftId` is unique.
- Enums: none.
- Concurrency: none.
- Sensitive data: learner reflection.
- Lifecycle: Created once; immutable.
- Indexes: unique `feedbackDraftId`; query `studentId, acknowledgedAt`.
- Retention: seven years after academic year closes.
- Delete behavior: restrict while feedback is retained.
- Audit: acknowledgement creation and denied acknowledgement attempts.
| Field | Type | Required | Nullable | Default | Constraints | Sensitive | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | UUID | yes | no | generated | PK, immutable UUIDv7 | internal | Acknowledgement identity. |
| feedbackDraftId | UUID | yes | no | none | FK FeedbackDraft.id; unique; must be Published | internal | Acknowledged feedback. |
| studentId | UUID | yes | no | actor id | FK UserProfile.id; must match assessment student | personal | Acknowledging student. |
| acknowledgedAt | timestamp | yes | no | generated UTC | immutable after creation | personal | Acknowledgement time. |
| reflection | string | no | yes | none | 0–500 characters | educational | Optional student reflection. |

## Relationships and delete behavior

`ClassGroup` has many `Enrollment` and `Assessment`; `Enrollment` has many `Assessment`; `Assessment` has one `FeedbackDraft`; `FeedbackDraft` has zero or one `FeedbackAcknowledgement`. Archived classes and inactive enrollments preserve history. Published feedback and acknowledgements are restricted from deletion.

## Indexes and query patterns

Class lists filter institution, lead teacher, status, and term. Rosters filter class and active enrollment. Staff assessment/review queries filter institution, class, student, status, and observation date. Student feedback queries filter `studentId` and published state, newest publication first.

## Lifecycle and state transitions

ClassGroup: Active → Archived. Enrollment: Active → Inactive. Assessment: Draft → FeedbackReady → Published. FeedbackDraft: NotRequested → PendingReview, NotRequested → Failed, Failed → PendingReview, PendingReview → Published. FeedbackAcknowledgement is created only for Published feedback and has no transition.

## Retention, privacy, and audit

Educational records are retained seven years after their academic year closes, then are disposed under the school data steward’s approved schedule. AI requests exclude student names, identifiers, and free-form historical records; only the current pseudonymous observation context is transferred. Create, generation, edit, publication, acknowledgement, and denial events are audit-recorded with actor, target, timestamp, outcome, and correlation identifier.
